<title>GERMANY: German post signs cooperation pact with Postbank.</title>
<headline>German post signs cooperation pact with Postbank.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>After months of negotiation, Germany's mail service, or Post AG, said on Tuesday it had signed a cooperation agreement with Postbank AG.</p>
<p>Details of the agreement were not disclosed. Post AG chief executive Klaus Zumwinkel said the agreement paved the way for the two firms to collaborate constructively in future.</p>
<p>The pact had been drafted by Germany's post ministry after talks between the two state-owned companies had failed.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
